   "description": "<p style=\"text-align: center;\">The AICLA NSW/ACT Division is pleased to invite you to our upcoming webinar, presented by Jonathan Liberis and Justin Khouri of Wotton + Kearney.</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">“Utmost Good Faith, Misrepresentation &amp; Non-Disclosure”</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">A common issue arising across all claim lines is the interplay between an insured&#8217;s, and insurer&#8217;s, duty of utmost good faith and misrepresentations or non-disclosures made prior to policy inception.</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">This presentation will examine the courts&#8217; current approach to these issues and explore the circumstances in which misrepresentations and non-disclosures can impact an insured&#8217;s entitlement under a policy. Attendees will gain valuable insight into the practical application of these principles and their relevance to claims handling.</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">Perfect for claims professionals, loss adjusters, brokers, underwriters, and anyone looking to strengthen their technical insurance knowledge.</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">&#x1f4c5; Wednesday, 21 October 2026<br /> &#x1f550; 1:00pm – 2:00pm AEDT<br /> &#x2705; Open to all AICLA members<br /> &#x2705; No cost to attend</p> <p style=\"text-align: center;\">AICLA CPD: 1 Point</p> <h2 style=\"text-align: center;\">To register and add this event to your calendar</h2> <h2 style=\"text-align: center;\"><a href=\"https://events.teams.microsoft.com/event/52ec7050-b5d5-",
